WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
- Today I'm going to be
reacting to some of the content

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.830
that's on my old phones.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.340
I went and got a couple of them out.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.560
One of them, I'm so upset,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.498
I cannot for the life of
me remember the passcode.

00:00:08.498 --> 00:00:10.300
I keep trying, but it says my phone is

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.490
disabled for 1,167 minutes.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.630
These kind of feel like a time capsule.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.628
It's like a portion of my life just frozen

00:00:17.628 --> 00:00:19.490
in phone form.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.250
A huge thank you to
LastPass for sponsoring

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.190
a portion of this video.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.940
And this could not be a better video to

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.204
integrate LastPass into because,

00:00:25.204 --> 00:00:27.800
one of the things, if you guys don't know,

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.780
I always have a lot of different phones.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.340
They even have this great feature where

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.610
if you don't want to come up with a

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.730
new unique password,

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.170
they'll make one for you!

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.740
So with LastPass, it will remember

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:37.710
all of my passwords.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.670
I'm able to quickly login to new phones,

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.970
and devices, and computers.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.670
It works on IOS, Android, Windows, Mac.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:44.503
I love LastPass,

00:00:44.503 --> 00:00:46.400
I've been using it for
the past couple of years.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.290
It's made it a lot
quicker and seamless when

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.570
I get a new phone to review.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.180
I just login to LastPass
and I instantly have access

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.201
to all of my accounts.

00:00:53.201 --> 00:00:54.480
So thank you LastPass

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.270
for sponsoring a portion of this video.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.030
Now I cannot wait to get into seeing

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.140
what's on my old phones.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.031
So these are the main phones

00:01:01.031 --> 00:01:02.607
we're going to be checking out today.

00:01:02.607 --> 00:01:05.090
This is the iPhone 6, which came out in

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:06.643
September of 2014.

00:01:06.643 --> 00:01:08.674
It's been my dream to be first in line

00:01:08.674 --> 00:01:10.325
for any Apple store event.

00:01:10.325 --> 00:01:12.210
This is it, like, we're here,

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.043
we're first.

00:01:13.043 --> 00:01:15.503
(crowd cheering)

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.843
This is the iPhone 6S
which came out in 2015.

00:01:22.843 --> 00:01:24.831
It's the day of the iPhone 6S launch,

00:01:24.831 --> 00:01:26.715
and puppy is not coming with us.

00:01:26.715 --> 00:01:28.260
You don't want to come.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.470
Well there's nobody else here, surprise.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.236
The middle of nowhere in North Carolina.

00:01:32.236 --> 00:01:33.952
First in line for the phone.

00:01:33.952 --> 00:01:35.402
Is anybody here yet?

00:01:35.402 --> 00:01:36.825
Open up, I'm ready.

00:01:36.825 --> 00:01:39.310
One of the newest features
is the force touch,

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.510
so you'll be able to
"peek in" as they said.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.008
They have definitely
seen some better days.

00:01:43.008 --> 00:01:46.010
I almost always have
had cases on my phones.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.650
So they're not in too bad of a condition.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.350
So let's first boot up the iPhone 6

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:51.470
and see what's on it.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.130
I did turn this on already,

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.650
and I didn't want to connect it to wifi

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.777
because I didn't want all
of these apps to update.

00:01:56.777 --> 00:02:00.870
This is the first page of my iPhone 6.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.750
The craziest part is seeing Vine on here.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.610
So just going through I feel like

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.610
I have a lot of the same sort of apps.

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:10.270
It's just funny to see like the old logos,

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.649
because obviously in 2014,

00:02:11.649 --> 00:02:13.280
a lot has changed since then.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.080
I guess this would be the end of 2015 then

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.393
when I got rid of this phone

00:02:17.393 --> 00:02:19.490
to upgrade to the iPhone 6S.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:20.660
The Aging Booth.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:21.629
The Ugly Booth.

00:02:21.629 --> 00:02:24.170
I used to go to Hot 8 Yoga all the time.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:25.910
Looks like I was still potentially,

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.220
maybe using Canon.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.197
Ship, that was a really
great shipping app.

00:02:29.197 --> 00:02:30.920
But they went under.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:31.753
Clash of Clans,

00:02:31.753 --> 00:02:33.360
oh my god I used to be obsessed.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.570
What I really want to see though

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:37.982
is what are some of the old
photos that I have on my phone.

00:02:37.982 --> 00:02:40.383
The last few photos that I have on here

00:02:40.383 --> 00:02:43.420
are me buying this phone.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:44.510
I was in North Carolina,

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.120
I remember I was on family vacation.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.030
So there it is.

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:48.583
Me buying the new phone.

00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:50.840
And there's my little Matty!

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:51.673
Oh my gosh,

00:02:51.673 --> 00:02:53.117
